/-!
# The infinite type-A Hecke algebra and its finite stages

For a commutative ring `R` and a unit `q : Rˣ`, the infinite type-A Hecke algebra
`InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q` is the associative unital `R`-algebra on generators `T i`,
`i : ℕ`, subject to

* the quadratic relation `T i * T i = (q - q⁻¹) • T i + 1`, equivalently
  `(T i - q) * (T i + q⁻¹) = 0`,
* the braid relation `T i * T (i + 1) * T i = T (i + 1) * T i * T (i + 1)`, and
* distant commutation `T i * T j = T j * T i` when `|i - j| ≥ 2`.

It is built as the quotient of `FreeAlgebra R ℕ` by these relations, which makes the universal
property `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.lift` available. The generator `T i` crosses the
strands `i` and `i + 1` (counted from `0`), so the algebra is the union of its stages
`TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.stage R q n`, each a quotient image of the Hecke algebra on `n`
strands. That these images are injective, so that the union is one of embedded copies, needs the
basis theorem and is not proved here. The algebra is the natural carrier of the Ocneanu trace,
which is a single linear functional on this union rather than a compatible family of functionals.

## Stages

The stage `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.stage R q n` is the subalgebra generated by the
first `n - 1` generators `T 0, …, T (n - 2)`, the image of the Hecke algebra on `n` strands. The
stages increase with `n` (`TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.stage_mono`), contain only scalars
on at most one strand (`TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.stage_eq_bot_of_le_one`), and exhaust
the algebra (`TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.iSup_stage`). The braid group on `n` strands
maps into the units of the algebra (`TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.braidHom`), with image in
the stage `n` (`TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.braidHom_mem_stage`), compatibly with adding a
last strand, and its image spans the stage as an `R`-module. That each stage is
isomorphic to the Hecke algebra presented on `n - 1` generators, equivalently that it is free of
rank `n!`, is the basis theorem and is not proved here.

As a submodule, the stage of the first `n + 2` strands is `Hₙ₊₁ + Hₙ₊₁ Tₙ Hₙ₊₁`, where `Hₙ₊₁` is
the stage of the first `n + 1` strands
(`TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.toSubmodule_stage_add_two`). This gives an induction
principle for submodules,
`TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.eq_top_of_algebraMap_mem_of_mul_T_mul_mem`, along which Markov
traces are computed recursively.

## Shifts and disjoint blocks

Shifting every strand index by `k` gives the algebra endomorphism
`TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.shift R q k`, `T i ↦ T (i + k)`. An element of the stage `a`
lives on the first `a` strands and the shift by `a` of any element lives on the strands from `a`
on, so the two commute (`TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.commute_shift_of_mem_stage`). Hence
placing an element of the stage `a` on the first `a` strands and an element of the stage `b` on
the next `b` strands is an algebra map from the tensor product
(`TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.blockIncl`). These are the disjoint block maps along which
Markov traces are multiplicative; that they are injective, so embeddings, needs the basis
theorem and is not proved here.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.Rel`: the defining relations on the free algebra.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra`: the infinite type-A Hecke algebra with parameter `q`.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.T`: the generators, and
  `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.unitT` the same generators as units.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.lift`: the universal property.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.stage`: the subalgebra of the first `n` strands.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.braidHom`: the homomorphism from the braid group on `n`
  strands to the units.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.shift`: the strand shift `T i ↦ T (i + k)`.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.blockIncl`: the disjoint block map of two stages.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.indexCharacter` and
  `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.signCharacter`: the characters `T i ↦ q` and `T i ↦ -q⁻¹`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.T_mul_self`, `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.T_braid` and
  `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.commute_T`: the defining relations.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.lift_T` and `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.hom_ext`:
  the universal property.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.iSup_stage` and
  `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.exists_mem_stage`: every element lies in a finite stage.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.toSubmodule_stage_add_two`: the decomposition
  `Hₙ₊₂ = Hₙ₊₁ + Hₙ₊₁ Tₙ Hₙ₊₁` of the stages.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.braidHom_strandIncl` and
  `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.span_range_braidHom`: the braid groups map compatibly into
  the stages and span them.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.commute_shift_of_mem_stage`: disjoint blocks commute.
* `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.algebraMap_injective` and
  `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.T_ne_algebraMap`: the presentation does not collapse.

## References

* V. F. R. Jones, *Hecke algebra representations of braid groups and link polynomials*,
  Ann. of Math. 126 (1987), 335–388, Sections 4 and 5 (the union of the Hecke algebras and the
  Ocneanu trace on it).
* The quotient presentation and universal-property API follow the construction pattern in
  `Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.CliffordAlgebra.Basic` and in `TauCeti.Algebra.TemperleyLieb.Basic`.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti

open scoped TensorProduct

variable (R : Type*) [CommRing R] (q : Rˣ)

namespace InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra

/-- The defining relations of the infinite type-A Hecke algebra with parameter `q`, as a relation
on the free algebra over the generators `ℕ`: the quadratic relation
`T i * T i = (q - q⁻¹) • T i + 1`, the braid relation for adjacent generators and commutation of
distant generators. The last one is imposed for one ordering of the pair, which suffices since the
quotient relation is symmetric. -/
inductive Rel : FreeAlgebra R ℕ → FreeAlgebra R ℕ → Prop
  | mul_self (i : ℕ) :
      Rel (FreeAlgebra.ι R i * FreeAlgebra.ι R i) (((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹) • FreeAlgebra.ι R i + 1)
  | braid (i : ℕ) :
      Rel (FreeAlgebra.ι R i * FreeAlgebra.ι R (i + 1) * FreeAlgebra.ι R i)
        (FreeAlgebra.ι R (i + 1) * FreeAlgebra.ι R i * FreeAlgebra.ι R (i + 1))
  | distant {i j : ℕ} (h : i + 2 ≤ j) :
      Rel (FreeAlgebra.ι R i * FreeAlgebra.ι R j) (FreeAlgebra.ι R j * FreeAlgebra.ι R i)

end InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra

/-- The infinite type-A Hecke algebra over `R` with parameter `q`: the free `R`-algebra on `ℕ`
modulo `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.Rel`. It is the union of its finite stages
`TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.stage R q n`; see the module docstring for what is proved about
them. -/
@[expose] def InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra : Type _ := RingQuot (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.Rel R q)

instance : Ring (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Ring (RingQuot (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.Rel R q)))

/-- The infinite type-A Hecke algebra over `R` is an algebra over every ring that `R` is an
algebra over. -/
instance (priority := 900) InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.instAlgebra' {S : Type*} [CommSemiring S]
    [Algebra S R] : Algebra S (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Algebra S (RingQuot (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.Rel R q)))

instance : Algebra R (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) := inferInstance

instance {S T : Type*} [CommSemiring S] [CommSemiring T] [SMul S T] [Algebra S R] [Algebra T R]
    [IsScalarTower S T R] : IsScalarTower S T (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsScalarTower S T (RingQuot (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.Rel R q)))

namespace InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra

/-- The quotient map from the free algebra to the infinite type-A Hecke algebra. -/
def mkAlgHom : FreeAlgebra R ℕ →ₐ[R] InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q :=
  RingQuot.mkAlgHom R (Rel R q)

variable {R}

/-- The generator `T i` of the infinite type-A Hecke algebra, the image of the elementary braid
crossing the strands `i` and `i + 1`. -/
def T (i : ℕ) : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q :=
  mkAlgHom R q (FreeAlgebra.ι R i)

variable {q}

/-- The quotient map takes each free-algebra generator to the corresponding Hecke generator. -/
@[simp]
theorem mkAlgHom_ι (i : ℕ) : mkAlgHom R q (FreeAlgebra.ι R i) = T q i := (rfl)

/-- Every element of the infinite type-A Hecke algebra is represented by a free-algebra
element. -/
theorem mkAlgHom_surjective : Function.Surjective (mkAlgHom R q) :=
  RingQuot.mkAlgHom_surjective _ _

/-- Related elements of the free algebra have the same image in the infinite type-A Hecke
algebra. -/
theorem mkAlgHom_rel {x y : FreeAlgebra R ℕ} (h : Rel R q x y) : mkAlgHom R q x = mkAlgHom R q y :=
  RingQuot.mkAlgHom_rel R h

/-- The quadratic relation of a Hecke generator. -/
@[simp]
theorem T_mul_self (i : ℕ) : T q i * T q i = ((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹) • T q i + 1 := by
  simpa only [map_mul, map_add, map_smul, map_one, mkAlgHom_ι] using
    mkAlgHom_rel (Rel.mul_self (q := q) i)

/-- The quadratic relation in factored form: each generator is annihilated by the polynomial with
roots `q` and `-q⁻¹`. -/
theorem T_sub_algebraMap_mul_T_add_algebraMap_eq_zero (i : ℕ) :
    (T q i - algebraMap R _ (q : R)) * (T q i + algebraMap R _ (↑q⁻¹ : R)) = 0 := by
  have hq : algebraMap R (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) (q : R) * algebraMap R _ (↑q⁻¹ : R) = 1 :=
    by simp [← map_mul]
  simp only [sub_mul, mul_add, T_mul_self, ← Algebra.commutes _ (T q i), hq,
    Algebra.smul_def, map_sub]
  abel

/-- Two generators on adjacent pairs of strands satisfy the braid relation. -/
theorem T_braid (i : ℕ) : T q i * T q (i + 1) * T q i = T q (i + 1) * T q i * T q (i + 1) := by
  simpa only [map_mul, mkAlgHom_ι] using mkAlgHom_rel (Rel.braid (R := R) (q := q) i)

/-- Two generators on disjoint pairs of strands commute. -/
theorem commute_T {i j : ℕ} (h : i + 2 ≤ j ∨ j + 2 ≤ i) : Commute (T q i) (T q j) := by
  rw [commute_iff_eq]
  rcases h with h | h
  · simpa only [map_mul, mkAlgHom_ι] using mkAlgHom_rel (Rel.distant (R := R) (q := q) h)
  · simpa only [map_mul, mkAlgHom_ι] using (mkAlgHom_rel (Rel.distant (R := R) (q := q) h)).symm

section Units

variable (q) in
/-- The generator `T i` as a unit. Its inverse is `T i - (q - q⁻¹)`, by the quadratic
relation. -/
def unitT (i : ℕ) : (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q)ˣ where
  val := T q i
  inv := T q i - algebraMap R _ ((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹)
  val_inv := by
    rw [mul_sub, ← Algebra.commutes, ← Algebra.smul_def, T_mul_self, add_sub_cancel_left]
  inv_val := by
    rw [sub_mul, ← Algebra.smul_def, T_mul_self, add_sub_cancel_left]

/-- The underlying element of `unitT q i` is the generator `T q i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem val_unitT (i : ℕ) : (unitT q i : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) = T q i := (rfl)

/-- The inverse of a generator is `T i - (q - q⁻¹)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem val_inv_unitT (i : ℕ) :
    (↑(unitT q i)⁻¹ : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) = T q i - algebraMap R _ ((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹) :=
  (rfl)

/-- Each generator of the infinite type-A Hecke algebra is a unit. -/
theorem isUnit_T (i : ℕ) : IsUnit (T q i) := (unitT q i).isUnit

end Units

section Lift

variable {A : Type*} [Semiring A] [Algebra R A]

/-- The universal property of the infinite type-A Hecke presentation: a sequence in an `R`-algebra
satisfying the quadratic relation, the braid relation for adjacent indices and commutation for
distant indices extends to an algebra map out of `InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q`. -/
def lift (f : ℕ → A) (hself : ∀ i, f i * f i = ((q : R) - ↑q⁻¹) • f i + 1)
    (hbraid : ∀ i, f i * f (i + 1) * f i = f (i + 1) * f i * f (i + 1))
    (hdist : ∀ {i j : ℕ}, i + 2 ≤ j → f i * f j = f j * f i) :
    InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q →ₐ[R] A :=
  RingQuot.liftAlgHom R ⟨FreeAlgebra.lift R f, by
    rintro x y (i | i | @⟨i, j, h⟩)
    · simpa only [map_mul, map_add, map_smul, map_one, FreeAlgebra.lift_ι_apply] using hself i
    · simpa only [map_mul, FreeAlgebra.lift_ι_apply] using hbraid i
    · simpa only [map_mul, FreeAlgebra.lift_ι_apply] using hdist h⟩

/-- The algebra map built by `TauCeti.InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra.lift` takes each generator to its
prescribed value. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_T (f : ℕ → A) (hself) (hbraid) (hdist) (i : ℕ) :
    lift (q := q) f hself hbraid hdist (T q i) = f i :=
  (RingQuot.liftAlgHom_mkAlgHom_apply R _ _ _).trans (FreeAlgebra.lift_ι_apply _ _)

/-- Two algebra maps out of the infinite type-A Hecke algebra agreeing on the generators are
equal. -/
@[ext high]
theorem hom_ext {F G : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q →ₐ[R] A} (h : ∀ i, F (T q i) = G (T q i)) :
    F = G :=
  RingQuot.ringQuot_ext' R F G <| FreeAlgebra.hom_ext (funext h)

end Lift

/-- The generators generate the infinite type-A Hecke algebra as an `R`-algebra. -/
theorem adjoin_range_T : Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range (T q)) = ⊤ := by
  have hrange : Set.range (T q) = mkAlgHom R q '' Set.range (FreeAlgebra.ι R (X := ℕ)) := by
    simp only [← Set.range_comp, Function.comp_def, mkAlgHom_ι]
  rw [hrange, ← AlgHom.map_adjoin, FreeAlgebra.adjoin_range_ι, Algebra.map_top]
  exact (AlgHom.range_eq_top _).2 mkAlgHom_surjective

section Stage

variable (R q) in
/-- The stage of the first `n` strands: the subalgebra generated by the generators
`T 0, …, T (n - 2)` that cross two of the strands `0, …, n - 1`. It is the image of the type-A
Hecke algebra on `n` strands. -/
def stage (n : ℕ) : Subalgebra R (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) :=
  Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range fun i : Fin (n - 1) ↦ T q i)

/-- A generator crossing two of the first `n` strands lies in the stage `n`. -/
theorem T_mem_stage {i n : ℕ} (h : i + 1 < n) : T q i ∈ stage R q n :=
  Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨⟨i, by omega⟩, rfl⟩

/-- The stage `n` is contained in a subalgebra exactly when every generator crossing two of the
first `n` strands is. -/
theorem stage_le_iff {n : ℕ} {S : Subalgebra R (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q)} :
    stage R q n ≤ S ↔ ∀ i, i + 1 < n → T q i ∈ S := by
  rw [stage, Algebra.adjoin_le_iff, Set.range_subset_iff]
  exact ⟨fun h i hi ↦ h ⟨i, by omega⟩, fun h i ↦ h i (by omega)⟩

/-- The stages increase with the number of strands. -/
theorem stage_mono : Monotone (stage R q) :=
  fun _ _ hmn ↦ stage_le_iff.2 fun _ hi ↦ T_mem_stage (by omega)

/-- On at most one strand there are no generators, so the stage consists of the scalars. -/
theorem stage_eq_bot_of_le_one {n : ℕ} (h : n ≤ 1) : stage R q n = ⊥ :=
  le_bot_iff.1 <| stage_le_iff.2 fun _ hi ↦ absurd hi (by omega)

/-- The stages exhaust the infinite type-A Hecke algebra. -/
theorem iSup_stage : ⨆ n, stage R q n = ⊤ := by
  rw [eq_top_iff, ← adjoin_range_T, Algebra.adjoin_le_iff, Set.range_subset_iff]
  exact fun i ↦ le_iSup (stage R q) (i + 2) (T_mem_stage (by omega))

/-- Every element of the infinite type-A Hecke algebra lies in some finite stage. -/
theorem exists_mem_stage (x : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) : ∃ n, x ∈ stage R q n := by
  have hx : x ∈ ((⨆ n, stage R q n : Subalgebra R _) : Set (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q)) := by
    rw [iSup_stage]
    trivial
  rwa [Subalgebra.coe_iSup_of_directed stage_mono.directed_le, Set.mem_iUnion] at hx

/-- A generator commutes with the stage of the first `n` strands when it crosses none of
them. -/
theorem commute_T_of_mem_stage {i n : ℕ} (h : n ≤ i) {x : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q}
    (hx : x ∈ stage R q n) : Commute (T q i) x :=
  Algebra.commute_of_mem_adjoin_of_forall_mem_commute hx <| by
    rintro _ ⟨j, rfl⟩
    exact commute_T (Or.inr (by omega))

end Stage

section Decomposition

/-! ### The decomposition `Hₙ₊₂ = Hₙ₊₁ + Hₙ₊₁ Tₙ Hₙ₊₁` of the stages -/

variable (R q) in
/-- The submodule `Hₙ₊₁ + Hₙ₊₁ Tₙ Hₙ₊₁` spanned by the stage of the first `n + 1` strands and
the products `a * T n * b` with `a`, `b` in that stage. -/
private def stageSplit (n : ℕ) : Submodule R (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) :=
  Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) ⊔
    Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) * (R ∙ T q n) *
      Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1))

private theorem mul_T_mul_mem_stageSplit {n : ℕ} {a b : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q}
    (ha : a ∈ stage R q (n + 1)) (hb : b ∈ stage R q (n + 1)) :
    a * T q n * b ∈ stageSplit R q n :=
  Submodule.mem_sup_right <| Submodule.mul_mem_mul
    (Submodule.mul_mem_mul ha (Submodule.mem_span_singleton_self _)) hb

private theorem stageSplit_le_iff {n : ℕ} {P : Submodule R (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q)} :
    stageSplit R q n ≤ P ↔ Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) ≤ P ∧
      ∀ a ∈ stage R q (n + 1), ∀ b ∈ stage R q (n + 1), a * T q n * b ∈ P := by
  refine sup_le_iff.trans <| and_congr_right fun _ ↦
    ⟨fun h a ha b hb ↦ h (Submodule.mul_mem_mul
      (Submodule.mul_mem_mul ha (Submodule.mem_span_singleton_self _)) hb), fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  refine Submodule.mul_le.2 fun y hy b hb ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_mul_span_singleton.1 hy
  exact h a ha b hb

/-- The stage `n + 2` lies in `Hₙ₊₁ + Hₙ₊₁ Tₙ Hₙ₊₁` as soon as `Tₙ Hₙ₊₁ Tₙ` does. -/
private theorem toSubmodule_stage_add_two_le_stageSplit {n : ℕ}
    (hT : ∀ a ∈ stage R q (n + 1), T q n * a * T q n ∈ stageSplit R q n) :
    Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 2)) ≤ stageSplit R q n := by
  have hS : Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) *
      Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) = Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) :=
    (Subalgebra.isIdempotentElem_toSubmodule _).eq
  -- The submodule is stable under multiplication by the stage `n + 1` on either side.
  have hleft : Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) * stageSplit R q n =
      stageSplit R q n := by
    simp only [stageSplit, Submodule.mul_sup, ← mul_assoc, hS]
  have hright : stageSplit R q n * Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) =
      stageSplit R q n := by
    simp only [stageSplit, Submodule.sup_mul, mul_assoc, hS]
  -- It is also stable under left multiplication by the last generator `T n`.
  have hTmul : ∀ m ∈ stageSplit R q n, T q n * m ∈ stageSplit R q n := by
    intro m hm
    obtain ⟨m₁, hm₁, m₂, hm₂, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.1 hm
    clear hm
    rw [mul_add]
    refine add_mem ?_ ?_
    · simpa only [one_mul] using mul_T_mul_mem_stageSplit (one_mem _) hm₁
    · induction hm₂ using Submodule.mul_induction_on' with
      | mem_mul_mem y hy b hb =>
        obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_mul_span_singleton.1 hy
        rw [← hright, ← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc]
        exact Submodule.mul_mem_mul (hT a ha) hb
      | add y _ y' _ hy hy' =>
        rw [mul_add]
        exact add_mem hy hy'
  -- Hence it is stable under left multiplication by the stage `n + 2`, and contains `1`.
  intro x hx
  rw [Subalgebra.mem_toSubmodule, stage] at hx
  suffices key : ∀ m ∈ stageSplit R q n, x * m ∈ stageSplit R q n by
    simpa only [mul_one] using key 1 (Submodule.mem_sup_left (one_mem (stage R q (n + 1))))
  induction hx using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hx
    dsimp only
    rcases (show (i : ℕ) < n ∨ (i : ℕ) = n by omega) with hi | hi
    · intro m hm
      rw [← hleft]
      exact Submodule.mul_mem_mul (T_mem_stage (by omega)) hm
    · intro m hm
      rw [hi]
      exact hTmul m hm
  | algebraMap r =>
    intro m hm
    rw [← Algebra.smul_def]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ r hm
  | add x y _ _ hx hy =>
    intro m hm
    rw [add_mul]
    exact add_mem (hx m hm) (hy m hm)
  | mul x y _ _ hx hy =>
    intro m hm
    rw [mul_assoc]
    exact hx _ (hy m hm)

/-- **The bimodule decomposition of the stages.** As a submodule, the stage of the first `n + 2`
strands is `Hₙ₊₁ + Hₙ₊₁ Tₙ Hₙ₊₁`: it is spanned by the stage `Hₙ₊₁` of the first `n + 1` strands
together with the products `a * T n * b` of the last generator with elements `a`, `b` of `Hₙ₊₁`.
This is the decomposition along which Markov traces are determined recursively. -/
theorem toSubmodule_stage_add_two (n : ℕ) :
    Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 2)) =
      Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) ⊔
        Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) * (R ∙ T q n) *
          Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ <| stageSplit_le_iff.2 ⟨fun x hx ↦ stage_mono (by omega) hx,
    fun a ha b hb ↦ (Subalgebra.mem_toSubmodule _).2 <| mul_mem
      (mul_mem (stage_mono (by omega) ha) (T_mem_stage (by omega))) (stage_mono (by omega) hb)⟩
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    refine toSubmodule_stage_add_two_le_stageSplit fun a ha ↦ ?_
    rw [stage_eq_bot_of_le_one le_rfl, Algebra.mem_bot] at ha
    obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := ha
    rw [← Algebra.commutes, mul_assoc, ← Algebra.smul_def, T_mul_self]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ r <| add_mem (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ <| by
      simpa only [one_mul, mul_one] using mul_T_mul_mem_stageSplit (one_mem _) (one_mem _))
      (Submodule.mem_sup_left (one_mem (stage R q 1)))
  | succ m ih =>
    -- Split `a ∈ Hₘ₊₂` as `Hₘ₊₁ + Hₘ₊₁ Tₘ Hₘ₊₁`; then `Tₘ₊₁` commutes past `Hₘ₊₁`.
    refine toSubmodule_stage_add_two_le_stageSplit fun a ha ↦ ?_
    let P : Submodule R (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) := (stageSplit R q (m + 1)).comap
      ((LinearMap.mulLeft R (T q (m + 1))).comp (LinearMap.mulRight R (T q (m + 1))))
    have hP : ∀ a, a ∈ P ↔ T q (m + 1) * a * T q (m + 1) ∈ stageSplit R q (m + 1) := fun a ↦ by
      simp only [P, Submodule.mem_comap, LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.mulLeft_apply,
        LinearMap.mulRight_apply, mul_assoc]
    refine (hP a).1 <| (ih.trans (stageSplit_le_iff.2 ⟨fun d hd ↦ (hP d).2 ?_,
      fun d hd e he ↦ (hP _).2 ?_⟩)) ha
    · rw [(commute_T_of_mem_stage le_rfl hd).eq, mul_assoc, T_mul_self, mul_add, mul_one,
        mul_smul_comm]
      refine add_mem (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ ?_)
        (Submodule.mem_sup_left (stage_mono (by omega) hd))
      simpa only [mul_one] using mul_T_mul_mem_stageSplit (stage_mono (by omega) hd) (one_mem _)
    · have hd' := (commute_T_of_mem_stage le_rfl hd).eq
      have he' := (commute_T_of_mem_stage le_rfl he).eq
      have h : T q (m + 1) * (d * T q m * e) * T q (m + 1) =
          d * T q m * T q (m + 1) * (T q m * e) := by
        calc _ = T q (m + 1) * d * T q m * (e * T q (m + 1)) := by simp only [mul_assoc]
          _ = d * (T q m * T q (m + 1) * T q m) * e := by
            rw [hd', ← he', T_braid]
            simp only [mul_assoc]
          _ = _ := by simp only [mul_assoc]
      rw [h]
      exact mul_T_mul_mem_stageSplit
        (mul_mem (stage_mono (by omega) hd) (T_mem_stage (by omega)))
        (mul_mem (T_mem_stage (by omega)) (stage_mono (by omega) he))

/-- To show that the stage of the first `n + 2` strands lies in a submodule, it suffices to check
the stage of the first `n + 1` strands and the products `a * T n * b` with `a`, `b` in it. -/
theorem toSubmodule_stage_add_two_le_iff {n : ℕ}
    {P : Submodule R (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q)} :
    Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 2)) ≤ P ↔
      Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) ≤ P ∧
        ∀ a ∈ stage R q (n + 1), ∀ b ∈ stage R q (n + 1), a * T q n * b ∈ P := by
  rw [toSubmodule_stage_add_two]
  exact stageSplit_le_iff

/-- **Induction along the stages.** A submodule of the infinite type-A Hecke algebra is everything
as soon as it contains the scalars and, whenever it contains the stage of the first `n + 1`
strands, it contains the products `a * T n * b` with `a`, `b` in that stage. -/
theorem eq_top_of_algebraMap_mem_of_mul_T_mul_mem
    {P : Submodule R (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q)} (h₀ : ∀ r, algebraMap R _ r ∈ P)
    (h : ∀ n, Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) ≤ P →
      ∀ a ∈ stage R q (n + 1), ∀ b ∈ stage R q (n + 1), a * T q n * b ∈ P) :
    P = ⊤ := by
  suffices hP : ∀ n, Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q (n + 1)) ≤ P by
    refine Submodule.eq_top_iff'.2 fun x ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨n, hx⟩ := exists_mem_stage x
    exact hP n (stage_mono (Nat.le_succ n) hx)
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    intro x hx
    rw [Subalgebra.mem_toSubmodule, stage_eq_bot_of_le_one le_rfl, Algebra.mem_bot] at hx
    obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := hx
    exact h₀ r
  | succ n ih => exact toSubmodule_stage_add_two_le_iff.2 ⟨ih, h n ih⟩

end Decomposition

section Braid

variable (R q) in
/-- The homomorphism from the braid group on `n` strands to the units of the infinite type-A
Hecke algebra, sending the elementary braid `σ i` to the generator `T i`. -/
def braidHom (n : ℕ) : BraidGroup n →* (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q)ˣ :=
  BraidGroup.lift (fun i ↦ unitT q i) (fun h ↦ Units.ext (commute_T h).eq)
    (fun {i j} h ↦ Units.ext <| by
      simp only [Units.val_mul, val_unitT]
      rcases h with h | h
      · rw [← h]
        exact T_braid _
      · rw [← h]
        exact (T_braid _).symm)

/-- The braid homomorphism sends each elementary braid to the corresponding generator. -/
@[simp]
theorem braidHom_sigma {n : ℕ} (i : Fin (n - 1)) :
    braidHom R q n (BraidGroup.sigma i) = unitT q i :=
  BraidGroup.lift_sigma _ _ _ i

/-- Adding an uncrossed last strand does not change the image of a braid: the braid
homomorphisms are compatible with the strand inclusions of the braid groups. -/
@[simp]
theorem braidHom_strandIncl {n : ℕ} (b : BraidGroup (n + 1)) :
    braidHom R q (n + 2) (BraidGroup.strandIncl b) = braidHom R q (n + 1) b := by
  have h : (braidHom R q (n + 2)).comp BraidGroup.strandIncl = braidHom R q (n + 1) :=
    BraidGroup.hom_ext fun i ↦ by simp
  exact DFunLike.congr_fun h b

/-- The image of a braid on `n` strands lies in the stage `n`. -/
theorem braidHom_mem_stage {n : ℕ} (b : BraidGroup n) :
    (braidHom R q n b : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) ∈ stage R q n := by
  -- Induct on `b` jointly with its inverse, since the inverse of a generator is not a generator.
  suffices h : (braidHom R q n b : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) ∈ stage R q n ∧
      (↑(braidHom R q n b)⁻¹ : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) ∈ stage R q n from h.1
  induction b using BraidGroup.sigma_induction_on with
  | sigma i =>
    have hi : T q i ∈ stage R q n := T_mem_stage (by omega)
    simp only [braidHom_sigma, val_unitT, val_inv_unitT]
    exact ⟨hi, sub_mem hi (Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ _)⟩
  | one => simp [one_mem]
  | mul b b' hb hb' =>
    simp only [map_mul, Units.val_mul, mul_inv_rev]
    exact ⟨mul_mem hb.1 hb'.1, mul_mem hb'.2 hb.2⟩
  | inv b hb => simpa only [map_inv, inv_inv] using hb.symm

/-- The images of the braids on `n` strands span the stage `n` as an `R`-module. -/
theorem span_range_braidHom (n : ℕ) :
    Submodule.span R (Set.range fun b ↦ (braidHom R q n b : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q)) =
      Subalgebra.toSubmodule (stage R q n) := by
  set M : Submonoid (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) :=
    MonoidHom.mrange ((Units.coeHom _).comp (braidHom R q n))
  have hM : (M : Set (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q)) =
      Set.range fun b ↦ (braidHom R q n b : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) := by
    simp [M, MonoidHom.coe_mrange, Function.comp_def]
  have hstage : stage R q n = Algebra.adjoin R (M : Set (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q)) := by
    refine le_antisymm (stage_le_iff.2 fun i hi ↦ Algebra.subset_adjoin ?_) ?_
    · exact ⟨BraidGroup.sigma ⟨i, by omega⟩, by simp⟩
    · rw [Algebra.adjoin_le_iff, hM, Set.range_subset_iff]
      exact braidHom_mem_stage
  rw [hstage, Algebra.adjoin_eq_span, Submonoid.closure_eq M, hM]

end Braid

section Shift

variable (R q) in
/-- The strand shift by `k`: the algebra endomorphism `T i ↦ T (i + k)` that moves every braid
`k` strands to the right. -/
def shift (k : ℕ) : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q →ₐ[R] InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q :=
  lift (fun i ↦ T q (i + k)) (fun _ ↦ T_mul_self _)
    (fun i ↦ by simpa only [Nat.add_right_comm i 1 k] using T_braid (q := q) (i + k))
    (fun h ↦ (commute_T (Or.inl (by omega))).eq)

/-- The strand shift by `k` sends `T i` to `T (i + k)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem shift_T (k i : ℕ) : shift R q k (T q i) = T q (i + k) :=
  lift_T _ _ _ _ i

/-- The strand shift by `0` is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem shift_zero : shift R q 0 = AlgHom.id R _ :=
  hom_ext fun i ↦ by simp

/-- Shifting by `b` and then by `a` is shifting by `a + b`. -/
@[simp]
theorem shift_shift (a b : ℕ) (x : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) :
    shift R q a (shift R q b x) = shift R q (a + b) x := by
  have h : (shift R q a).comp (shift R q b) = shift R q (a + b) :=
    hom_ext fun i ↦ by simp only [AlgHom.comp_apply, shift_T, Nat.add_assoc, Nat.add_comm b a]
  exact DFunLike.congr_fun h x

/-- The strand shift by `k` moves the stage `n` into the stage `n + k`. -/
theorem shift_mem_stage {n : ℕ} (k : ℕ) {x : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q}
    (hx : x ∈ stage R q n) : shift R q k x ∈ stage R q (n + k) := by
  have h : stage R q n ≤ (stage R q (n + k)).comap (shift R q k) :=
    stage_le_iff.2 fun i hi ↦ by
      rw [Subalgebra.mem_comap, shift_T]
      exact T_mem_stage (by omega)
  exact h hx

/-- The image of the strand shift by `k` is generated by the generators `T (i + k)`. -/
theorem shift_mem_adjoin (k : ℕ) (x : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) :
    shift R q k x ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range fun i ↦ T q (i + k)) := by
  have hx : x ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range (T q)) := by
    rw [adjoin_range_T]
    trivial
  have hmap : shift R q k x ∈ (Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range (T q))).map (shift R q k) :=
    Subalgebra.mem_map.2 ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  rwa [AlgHom.map_adjoin, ← Set.range_comp, Function.comp_def, funext (shift_T k)] at hmap

/-- **Disjoint blocks commute.** An element of the stage `a`, living on the first `a` strands,
commutes with the shift by `a` of any element, which lives on the strands from `a` on. -/
theorem commute_shift_of_mem_stage {a : ℕ} {x : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q}
    (hx : x ∈ stage R q a) (y : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) : Commute x (shift R q a y) := by
  refine (Algebra.commute_of_mem_adjoin_of_forall_mem_commute hx ?_).symm
  rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
  refine (Algebra.commute_of_mem_adjoin_of_forall_mem_commute (shift_mem_adjoin a y) ?_).symm
  rintro _ ⟨j, rfl⟩
  exact commute_T (Or.inl (by omega))

variable (R q) in
/-- The disjoint block map: the algebra map from the tensor product of the stages `a` and `b` to
the stage `a + b` that places the first factor on the first `a` strands and the second factor,
shifted by `a`, on the next `b` strands. Its injectivity, which would make it an embedding,
needs the basis theorem and is not proved here. -/
def blockIncl (a b : ℕ) : stage R q a ⊗[R] stage R q b →ₐ[R] stage R q (a + b) :=
  (Algebra.TensorProduct.lift (stage R q a).val ((shift R q a).comp (stage R q b).val)
    fun x y ↦ by
      rw [AlgHom.comp_apply, Subalgebra.val_apply, Subalgebra.val_apply]
      exact commute_shift_of_mem_stage x.2 y).codRestrict _ fun z ↦ by
    induction z using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
    | tmul x y =>
      rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.lift_tmul, AlgHom.comp_apply, Subalgebra.val_apply,
        Subalgebra.val_apply]
      refine mul_mem (stage_mono (Nat.le_add_right a b) x.2) ?_
      rw [Nat.add_comm a b]
      exact shift_mem_stage a y.2
    | add z z' hz hz' => simpa only [map_add] using add_mem hz hz'

/-- The disjoint block map multiplies the first factor by the shift of the second. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_blockIncl_tmul {a b : ℕ} (x : stage R q a) (y : stage R q b) :
    (blockIncl R q a b (x ⊗ₜ y) : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) = x * shift R q a y := by
  rw [blockIncl, AlgHom.coe_codRestrict, Algebra.TensorProduct.lift_tmul, AlgHom.comp_apply,
    Subalgebra.val_apply, Subalgebra.val_apply]

end Shift

section Characters

variable (R q) in
/-- The index character of the infinite type-A Hecke algebra, the algebra map to the base ring
sending every generator to the eigenvalue `q`. -/
def indexCharacter : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q →ₐ[R] R :=
  lift (fun _ ↦ (q : R)) (fun _ ↦ by simp [smul_eq_mul, sub_mul]) (fun _ ↦ rfl) (fun _ ↦ rfl)

variable (R q) in
/-- The sign character of the infinite type-A Hecke algebra, the algebra map to the base ring
sending every generator to the eigenvalue `-q⁻¹`. -/
def signCharacter : InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q →ₐ[R] R :=
  lift (fun _ ↦ -(↑q⁻¹ : R)) (fun _ ↦ by simp [smul_eq_mul, sub_mul]) (fun _ ↦ rfl)
    (fun _ ↦ rfl)

/-- The index character sends each generator to `q`. -/
@[simp]
theorem indexCharacter_T (i : ℕ) : indexCharacter R q (T q i) = q :=
  lift_T _ _ _ _ i

/-- The sign character sends each generator to `-q⁻¹`. -/
@[simp]
theorem signCharacter_T (i : ℕ) : signCharacter R q (T q i) = -(↑q⁻¹ : R) :=
  lift_T _ _ _ _ i

/-- The base ring embeds into the infinite type-A Hecke algebra. -/
theorem algebraMap_injective :
    Function.Injective (algebraMap R (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q)) :=
  fun x y hxy ↦ by simpa using congrArg (indexCharacter R q) hxy

instance [Nontrivial R] : Nontrivial (InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra R q) :=
  algebraMap_injective.nontrivial

/-- A generator is not a scalar when the two eigenvalues `q` and `-q⁻¹` are distinct. -/
theorem T_ne_algebraMap (hq : (q : R) ≠ -↑q⁻¹) (i : ℕ) (r : R) : T q i ≠ algebraMap R _ r :=
  fun h ↦ hq <| by
    rw [← indexCharacter_T i, ← signCharacter_T i, h, AlgHom.commutes, AlgHom.commutes]

end Characters

end InfiniteTypeAHeckeAlgebra

end TauCeti
